# Source Servings: 6
# Conversion note: 12 ham slices listed, method uses one on each of six sandwiches; 180° has no explicit scale. No invented use for remaining ham or explicit Celsius attribution.

::ingredients

# Béchamel
(butter) 50g
(flour) 50g
(milk) 1 litre
(salt) to taste
(pepper, ground) to taste
(nutmeg) a pinch
# Bites
(bread) 12 slices
(mustard) 2tbsp
(ham, very thin slices, with Italian herbs) 12 slices
(cheese, grated, Emmental or Comté or Gruyère or Mimolette) 80g

::equipment

(saucepan, heavy-bottomed)
(whisk)
(oven)
(baking sheet)
(aluminium foil)

::instructions

{béchamel} = (butter) <melt, heavy-bottomed saucepan>
    + (flour) + (salt) + (pepper) + (nutmeg) <mix, as soon as butter foams>
    + (milk) <pour, little by little, whisk each time, until sauce thickens>
(oven) <preheat, th. 6 / 180°>
(baking sheet) <remove, from oven> <line, aluminium foil>
(bread) 6 slices <lay out>
    + (mustard) <spread, a little>
    + {béchamel} <spread, layer>
    + (ham) <place, 1 slice folded in 4 on each>
    + (cheese) some <sprinkle>
    + {béchamel} <spread, layer>
    + (bread) remaining 6 slices <top>
    + {béchamel} <spread, thin layer>
    + (cheese) rest of <distribute>
{sandwiches} <arrange, baking sheet> <bake, ~10m>
Optional [
    {sandwiches} <broil, 3-4m at end>
]

